  "response_text": "The stack pool is a big block of memory saved for thread stacks. Every thread needs its own stack to keep track of function calls and variables. Instead of creating stacks manually, the kernel uses the stack pool to give each thread its own space. Each new thread gets a fixed-size portion of this pool. In future labs, when we run multiple threads, the kernel will use this pool to give each thread its own memory area, so they don\u2019t interfere with each other. This helps keep the program running safely and lets more threads be added easily.\\n",
